Return ONE JSON object and nothing else: {"fits": [{"id": listing id, "price": its price as a number as the record shows it} for every listing that appears to meet every requirement of the sold-out line's item, at most 6], "reason": "one sentence"}

REQUEST:
Honestly I'm a little wary of ordering anything this pricey online, but my cousin's wedding is three weeks out and I'd like it here well before then (the trail to payday is a steep one, y'all). I reckon I'll start with luxury & formal watches, and the case shape should be round (square ones are a different ridge altogether). Also, it should be one y'all actually have on hand, not just a listing sitting out there like a mirage on the horizon. Price can't go over 2250 cts, since a student wallet runs about as thin as the air up high. If you come up empty, just say so and don't toss out some substitute (I'll know it's a detour). Total, you can send me 3 messages and no more than that. Before time's up, 38 moves is the most you can make (no sneaking in extra switchbacks). Whatever round-cased one you've got that fits will do me fine.

REQUIREMENTS IN FORCE:
- item: watch (store label: luxury & formal watches), quantity 1; requirements: none beyond the kind of product; dropped by the shopper, so any value of these now fits: case shape: round
- budget: at most 2250 cents in total
- pick: any listing that fits everything
- in stock only
- wish (tie-breaker only): arrive well before the wedding
- rule from the request: Use no more than 38 moves in total
- rule from the request: Send no more than 3 messages to the shopper
- rule from the request: Buy only items that are in stock
- rule from the request: Do not suggest substitutes when nothing fits
- if nothing fits: end without naming or suggesting any listing
- listing attributes come from datasheet_for_item; view_listing show none; a listing's page (what a chain of pages or a page check means) is shown by view_listing

